prefix (wasm): the filesystem root is a local prefix only when pnpm runs there (homescoop)

pnpm's local prefix is the nearest ancestor of the cwd with a project
marker, node_modules among them. In slicc the root holds the base set's
/node_modules, so every directory without a manifest of its own resolved
to `/`: `pnpm add is-odd` in /home scaffolded /package.json (name "",
written to /.tmpXXXXXX, 214 bytes), failed with
ERR_PNPM_PACKAGE_MANIFEST_IO_ERROR "initialize the state: No such file or
directory (os error 44)", and left the temp file at `/`. Had it gone
through, it would have installed into slicc's base set. Native pnpm
creates package.json in the cwd there (no ancestor has a marker). On
wasm the walk stops below the root, and the cwd is the prefix; a command
run in `/` itself still acts on `/`.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: slicc's base set no longer lives in /node_modules, or
upstream's wasm build stops the prefix walk below the root.

--- a/pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/prefix.rs
+++ b/pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/prefix.rs
@@ -82,6 +82,13 @@
     let mut current = name.to_path_buf();
 
     loop {
+        // In a WebContainer the filesystem root holds the runtime's own
+        // node_modules (slicc's base set), so it would end every walk: a
+        // command in a directory without a project would act on `/`. The
+        // root is a prefix only when the command runs there.
+        if cfg!(target_family = "wasm") && current != original && current.parent().is_none() {
+            return Ok(original.to_path_buf());
+        }
         match probe_project_markers(&current, targets, original)? {
             MarkerProbe::Found => return Ok(current),
             MarkerProbe::Unreadable => return Ok(original.to_path_buf()),
